WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:05.830
<i>Main tries to create various colored inks with 
the daughter of the ink workshop foreman, Heidi.</i>

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.430
<i>Meanwhile at the cathedral, 
they take in an abandoned child</i>

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.060
<i>and name him Dirk.</i>

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:16.580
Ugh! Why do I have to do this, too?

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.600
Of course, you should look after him.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.970
You're going to be this 
child's older sister.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.910
O-Older sister?

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.180
Yes. I would like for you to care for this 
child like he's your own flesh and blood.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:35.170
Did you see that? Dirk smiled at me!

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.140
<i>However...</i>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.230
What are these spots?

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.400
He feels so hot...

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.260
What a terrible fever... but why?

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.050
Dirk...

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.580
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.090
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:29.000
<b>Chapter Thirty-Three
Delia and Dirk</b>

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.490
Dirk's cheeks had bumps on them?

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.760
Yes. They went away immediately 
when I gave him goat's milk.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.020
I saw them on him this morning.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.830
Is this common with babies?

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.100
He seems to be okay right now.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.310
He really had bumps on his face!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.570
I can't really determine anything 
unless I see them myself.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.310
Let's see what happens the 
next time you give him milk.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.040
I believe he's getting hungry.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.300
I'm sorry, Dirk. We'll give you 
some milk in a little bit.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.440
A fever?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.670
Yes, Lady Main. He's burning up.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.020
<i>This is...</i>

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.630
Please look.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.030
He has bumps on his cheeks.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:53.430
Yes, I see that. Delia, go ahead
 and give him some milk.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.530
All right.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.560
Here you go, Dirk.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.470
The bumps disappeared.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.190
What could this mean?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.430
Fran, could you fetch Lutz for me?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.020
Could you also request a 
meeting with the head priest?

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:22.760
As soon as possible.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.450
As you wish.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.660
Lady Main, did you figure something out?

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.200
I cannot say yet.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.840
Fran said you wanted to talk to me.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.110
What's the matter, Main?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.230
Yes, well...

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:03.930
I was wondering if you'd go to the 
forest and get me some tau fruit.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.300
Tau fruit?

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.240
Yes. Please, Lutz.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.610
All right.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:20.570
<i>If we have tau fruits, we can keep Dirk's
 mana from going berserk and killing him.</i>

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.450
What is it now?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.590
The baby I told you about yesterday...

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.850
Are we safe talking about this here?

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:37.070
So this must be important if you're worried 
about who might be watching or listening.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.290
Yes.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.610
Did something happen to this baby?

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.750
I believe the baby has the Devouring.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.520
When crying from hunger,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.250
the baby develops a fever
and breaks out in a rash.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.370
But after taking milk, the fever goes away 
and the baby returns to normal.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.960
If the child is showing that
many signs as an infant,

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.720
an abundance of mana must be present.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:10.630
I knew it.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.810
The infant definitely has the Devouring.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.470
<i>He's thinking about something.</i>

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.780
It might be best if we have the child form 
a contract with a noble immediately.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.030
Huh? A contract?

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.560
The baby will not survive otherwise.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.270
What it means to form a 
contract with noble is

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.670
in exchange for the noble giving 
the other magic items to survive,

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.560
they become the noble's subordinate,

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.550
have their mana drained away,

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.310
and will live that life of confinement 
until they literally die.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.510
Head Priest, is there any 
way we can have Dirk

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:58.050
offer up mana and become 
a blue-robed priest like me?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.930
Raising a child as a blue-robed
 priest costs money.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.450
Who, exactly, would pay for that?

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.000
Well...

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.860
Even if you could pay,

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:12.530
wouldn't you be favoring one child over 
the others as the head of the orphanage?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.210
Without magic items, those 
with the Devouring will die.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.210
Forming a contract with a noble 
is absolutely necessary.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.200
Right...

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.180
Mostly, those who form 
contracts with Devouring children

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.280
are nobles who feel like 
their mana is lacking.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.580
They don't usually want others to 
know they've made this contact,

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:39.090
so they often have them become 
concubines or attendants.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.360
<i>Just like Freida...</i>

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.720
But it's different when 
it comes to adopting them.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.730
Then, they need permission from the parents.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:50.660
It's not as though they can form 
these contracts with anyone.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.610
Then what about me?

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.350
In your case, because of 
your abundance of mana,

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.760
the fact that you are smart 
enough to make your own money,

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.640
and know how to use your own talents,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.630
we decided it'd be best if you were 
adopted by an upper-class noble.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.540
<i>I see...</i>

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.260
Head Priest,

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:15.390
please make sure you find 
Dirk a good candidate.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.200
Main, is this infant a girl?

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.870
He's a boy.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:23.580
Him being a boy makes this more difficult.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:28.030
If he was a girl, he might've had 
a better chance of being adopted.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.670
<i>You mean as a pawn in a 
marriage of convenience.</i>

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:37.920
Whatever the outcome may be, we need to find 
out how much mana this infant has first.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:49.170
The head priest is going to find out 
how much mana you have tomorrow.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.930
Good morning, Head Priest.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.930
Where is this child?

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.550
Right this way.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:25.140
Thank you kindly for coming to see us.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.000
Main, see everyone else out of the room.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:27.930
Understood.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.560
I need all of you to leave for now.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:04.370
Oh, the color is changing.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.760
Hm... He's about equal to a 
stronger middle-class noble.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:18.150
If a noble is lacking mana right now,
 they may want to adopt him.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.590
But if we think about your safety,

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:25.530
it's unwise to probe around 
too much for possible interest.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:33.920
If you're that worried, then once 
you're adopted by Karstedt,

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.270
you should be the one to form 
a contract with this child.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.590
Me?

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:41.180
You'd be a noble, so it would be possible.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.050
Thank you kindly!

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.860
Main, how many know that this 
child has the Devouring?

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.550
Just me.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:56.030
In that case, continue to stay quiet 
about that and take care of him.

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:01.940
The high priest will take advantage
 of this if he finds out about it.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.500
Between you, who can be rather disobedient, 
and this child who cannot think for himself yet,

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.120
it's clear which one the 
high priest would choose.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:13.390
If you want to protect him, 
make sure he is not found out.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.610
Whether or not you are able 
to protect this infant

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.830
may greatly change your position 
and your surroundings.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.120
Always keep that in mind.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:23.820
Yes.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.360
Lady Main, what did the head priest say?

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.830
Is Dirk ill?

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:40.810
No, he is fine.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:44.040
He just said to continue to look 
after Dirk at the orphanage.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.130
I see...

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.090
Oh, thank goodness.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.900
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.990
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.360
Morning, miss. I've been waiting for you.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.550
Good morning, Heidi.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.710
We wrote down the results 
from all of our experiments.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.270
Nah, it's okay. I can't really read anyway.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.970
More importantly, how'd the results turn out?

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:30.110
We found out that linseed produced 
blues, mische produced greens,

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:33.600
and that eise produces yellows.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.310
Well done, Miss!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:41.230
Today, let's start using the ink we've 
made on vorlin paper and trombe paper.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.540
The colors pretty much end 
up as-is on the trombe paper.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.260
They end up a bit darker on the vorlin paper.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.710
Hopefully they stay like 
this even after they dry.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.510
No way...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.410
They darkened way more after they dried.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.170
It would be great for drawing blood, though!

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:12.850
No one needs a specific ink just for that.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:19.730
Now I know why art workshops 
keep how paint is made a secret.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.410
Apparently paint is made very 
specifically by certain workshops,

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.160
but the methods they use are kept a secret.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.600
You basically won't find any 
paint available where I live.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.250
Paints for nobles are made by the
 workshop they ordered them from,

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.540
and delivered right to them.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:40.410
Miss! Let's find out why 
the inks change color!

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.680
All that matters is the result!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.250
Okay, next, let's try 
combining the colors, Gil.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.870
Okay, Lady Main.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:10.400
I guess it's not great that all the colors 
turned black when you combined them.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.790
Seriously, what should I do?

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.400
You're not using a fixing agent?

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.030
Fixing agent?

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:21.350
It's a liquid used to make 
sure the color stays.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:25.870
When you're dying fabrics, you use it to 
make sure the color doesn't change any more.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.210
Thanks, Mom! I'll give that a try.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:34.180
So there's something called 
a fixing agent, huh?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.960
I guess we would've never 
figured that out if Missus Effa

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.890
didn't work at a fabric dying workshop.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.310
Once we gather all the ingredients, 
I'm going to try to make some.

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.780
My mom told me how to make it.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:50.400
You just need to tell us how to make it.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:52.860
We'll make it for you!

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.660
You're not allowed to, Lady Main.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.460
Oh, also... Could you get 
some parchment from Wilma?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:04.300
I'll get things ready at the 
workshop, so we can print.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:11.420
So as you can see, I'm being left out,

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.840
and Gil and Lutz are off making 
the fixing agent somewhere.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.000
Isn't that mean?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.560
Oh, Lady Main.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.440
A fixing agent is absolutely 
necessary when drawing or painting.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.400
Wilma always mentions it's impossible 
to paint or draw without it.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.200
Huh?

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.800
You always seem to know the 
most surprising things,

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.190
but you had no idea about fixing agents.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.370
Just a little more, Dirk. Don't give up!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.330
Dirk can already flip over?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.000
No, not yet.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.590
He's almost got it though.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:52.080
That's quite fast. My little 
Kamil's nowhere near that.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:59.000
Well done, my little brother. 
You're quite talented.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.410
What's with that adorable smile?!

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.270
I've never seen that before!

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:06.180
Lady Main.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:11.040
Leave Dirk to Delia and let 
us start this harspiel lesson.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:16.600
Good morning, Lady Main. 
I've come to take Dirk.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:20.570
Good morning, Wilma. Thank you again.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:25.500
How was last night, Delia?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.000
The same as usual, Wilma.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.740
I'll go ahead and take Dirk.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:32.990
When Dirk leaves, I get so lonely.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:38.140
Okay, off you go.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:54.400
Lady Main, do you think Dirk 
feels lonely or is crying?

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.870
He's surrounded by other children, 
so I'm sure he's not lonely.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.330
Even if he may not be able to 
sleep because it's too loud.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.580
But that's not fair to Dirk.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:07.530
Well, Wilma will look after him.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:09.500
How do we know that, though?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:16.220
Ugh! Are you even listening to me, Lady Main?

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:20.230
Well, if you're that worried, 
why don't you see for yourself?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.610
I don't want to go to the orphanage!

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.110
Make sure you two get plenty of rest.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.890
Please excuse us.

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:49.110
Excuse us.

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.600
Sir Damuel.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.310
I'm going to head to the orphanage.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:00.850
Hey, Apprentice Priestess.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:03.220
Where are your attendants?

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.180
Huh?

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.430
Why are you trying to leave 
without a single escort?

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.910
Perfect timing.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:14.990
You, attendant. Go with 
Lady Main to the orphanage.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:16.000
Huh?

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.590
Just to the entrance of 
the orphanage will do.

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:21.230
Do you think you'll be able to?

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:24.760
As you wish.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.800
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:41.700
Hey.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:45.900
Are you implying that the apprentice 
priestess, your master, should open the door?

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.560
Open the door.

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.380
Good work, you two.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:28.590
Lady Main, I'm going to head back.

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:31.170
All right. Sorry to push you like this.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.650
Thank you, Delia.

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:34.880
It's all right.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.070
Dirk!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:48.530
Seriously! What if Dirk got hurt?!

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:51.030
You need to keep a better eye on him!

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.350
Lady Main, do you think 
Delia will be all right?

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.560
I heard that she didn't like 
coming to the orphanage.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.480
I'm not sure.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:13.620
But I'm hoping she'll let Dirk's 
cuteness get to her little by little.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.930
<i>This isn't the same place 
you came from anymore, Delia.</i>

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.410
Ugh, what's that supposed to mean?!

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:44.800
That's Delia's voice.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.380
I wonder what happened.

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:49.140
Let's hurry back, Apprentice Priestess.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.230
The head priest can't be trusted!

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.410
He can be trusted.

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:56.890
Fran, Delia.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:58.700
What's this all about?

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:04.450
Lady Main, is it true that Dirk 
is supposed to be adopted?

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:43.050
<b>Next Chapter
Ominous Developments</b>

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:48.850
Head Priest, I thought that Dirk 
actually had more mana than I do.

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:52.350
At the time of your births, 
Dirk's would probably measure higher.

00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:54.520
This doesn't apply to the original Main,

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:58.550
but after you took over her consciousness 
and your mana condensed,

00:22:58.550 --> 00:23:00.960
your mana capacity vastly increased.

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:02.750
This must be it.

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Mana</b>

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:04.350
When you compress mana,

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:07.770
it creates empty space for your body's
mana to fill, so you compress it tighter,

00:23:07.770 --> 00:23:09.950
and then you get even more space.

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:14.360
Yes. This is a method of controlling mana 
that you learn at the royal academy.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:16.810
What? Really?

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:19.410
Here I was barely surviving.

00:23:19.770 --> 00:23:23.230
I'm sure some harm may come from this.

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:25.490
Wh-What do you mean by harm?

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:29.430
I'll tell you if you go to the royal academy.

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:31.010
What?

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:34.830
Tell me now, Head Priest!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
